                <pb facs="0242" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23610: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dyer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-20T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 17, 9 a.m.</p>
                <p>Department does not feel that emergency necessitating asylum in United States for
                    Chinese in your district is likely to arise.</p>
                <p>Post office Department has instructed Postmasters Naco, Douglas and Nogales to
                    hold mail for Americans in Sonora until necessary arrangements have been made
                    for its delivery.</p>
                <p>Department has received no request from Mexican Government for permission to
                    transport armed forces to Sonora via American territory.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
